    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d47">

                <pb facs="0208" n="188" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg188"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1008.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-06-27"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 27, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of the 10th of June, No. 715,
                    has been received, together with copies of Earl Russell’s notes addressed to you
                    of the 7th of May and the 1st of June. I observe that orators in Parliament
                    complain that the legislature and people of Great Britain are left by the
                    ministry in ignorance of the state of the question which is under debate in the
                    European conference now sitting in London.</p>
                <p>If the British people form an opinion concerning enlistments in England in
                    violation of the neutrality laws from the debates in the House of Lords, they
                    must come to the conclusion that it is not Great Britain that is injuring the
                    United States, but the United States that are invading the sovereignty of Great
                    Britain in that way. They will of course be undeceived when the correspondence
                    of the two governments shall come to light. I give you, herewith, a copy of a
                    resolution of the Senate on that subject, and of the President’s answer to the
                    Senate.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM II. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
